<h1>SECTION B — Spring Security, End to End</h1>
<h2 id="p7-b1-the-mental-model">B1. The mental model<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p7-b1-the-mental-model">#</a></h2>
<p>Security is a chain of <strong>servlet filters</strong> installed ahead of <code>DispatcherServlet</code> via a single <code>DelegatingFilterProxy</code> ("springSecurityFilterChain") that delegates to a <code>FilterChainProxy</code>, which picks the matching <code>SecurityFilterChain</code>.</p>
<p><strong>The filter order (know roughly this sequence):</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><code>DisableEncodeUrlFilter</code></li>
<li><code>WebAsyncManagerIntegrationFilter</code></li>
<li><code>SecurityContextHolderFilter</code> — loads the <code>SecurityContext</code> (from session, or nothing if stateless)</li>
<li><code>HeaderWriterFilter</code> — security headers</li>
<li><code>CorsFilter</code></li>
<li><code>CsrfFilter</code></li>
<li><code>LogoutFilter</code></li>
<li>Authentication filters — <code>UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter</code>, <code>BearerTokenAuthenticationFilter</code>, <code>OAuth2LoginAuthenticationFilter</code></li>
<li><code>RequestCacheAwareFilter</code></li>
<li><code>AnonymousAuthenticationFilter</code></li>
<li><code>SessionManagementFilter</code></li>
<li><code>ExceptionTranslationFilter</code> — turns <code>AuthenticationException</code> → 401 entry point, <code>AccessDeniedException</code> → 403</li>
<li><code>AuthorizationFilter</code> (was <code>FilterSecurityInterceptor</code>) — the final gate</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>The authentication flow:</strong>
<code>Filter</code> → builds an unauthenticated <code>Authentication</code> token → <code>AuthenticationManager</code> (<code>ProviderManager</code>) → iterates <code>AuthenticationProvider</code>s → <code>DaoAuthenticationProvider</code> calls <code>UserDetailsService.loadUserByUsername</code> → compares with <code>PasswordEncoder.matches</code> → returns an authenticated <code>Authentication</code> with authorities → stored in <code>SecurityContextHolder</code> (a <code>ThreadLocal</code>).</p>
<h2 id="p7-b2-modern-configuration-boot-3-security-6">B2. Modern configuration (Boot 3 / Security 6)<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p7-b2-modern-configuration-boot-3-security-6">#</a></h2>
<p><code>WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter</code> is <strong>removed</strong>. You declare beans:</p>
<div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="nd">@Configuration</span>
<span class="nd">@EnableWebSecurity</span>
<span class="nd">@EnableMethodSecurity</span><span class="w">          </span><span class="c1">// was @EnableGlobalMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)</span>
<span class="kd">public</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">class</span> <span class="nc">SecurityConfig</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nd">@Bean</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="n">SecurityFilterChain</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nf">api</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">HttpSecurity</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">http</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">throws</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Exception</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="k">return</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">http</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">securityMatcher</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/api/**"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">csrf</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">AbstractHttpConfigurer</span><span class="p">::</span><span class="n">disable</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w">              </span><span class="c1">// safe only because we're stateless + token auth</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">cors</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">Customizer</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">withDefaults</span><span class="p">())</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">sessionManagement</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">s</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">s</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">sessionCreationPolicy</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">SessionCreationPolicy</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">STATELESS</span><span class="p">))</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">authorizeHttpRequests</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">auth</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">auth</span>
<span class="w">          </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">requestMatchers</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/api/auth/**"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">"/actuator/health/**"</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">permitAll</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="w">          </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">requestMatchers</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">HttpMethod</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">GET</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">"/api/markets/**"</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">hasAuthority</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"SCOPE_market:read"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="w">          </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">requestMatchers</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/api/admin/**"</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">hasRole</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"ADMIN"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="w">          </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">anyRequest</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="na">authenticated</span><span class="p">())</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">oauth2ResourceServer</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">o</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">o</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">jwt</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">j</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">j</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">jwtAuthenticationConverter</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">converter</span><span class="p">())))</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">exceptionHandling</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">e</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">-&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">e</span>
<span class="w">          </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">authenticationEntryPoint</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">restAuthEntryPoint</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w">   </span><span class="c1">// 401 JSON, not a login redirect</span>
<span class="w">          </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">accessDeniedHandler</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">restAccessDeniedHandler</span><span class="p">))</span><span class="w">  </span><span class="c1">// 403 JSON</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">build</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="p">}</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nd">@Bean</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">PasswordEncoder</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nf">passwordEncoder</span><span class="p">()</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">return</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">BCryptPasswordEncoder</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">12</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">}</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nd">@Bean</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">AuthenticationManager</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nf">authManager</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">AuthenticationConfiguration</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">c</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">throws</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Exception</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="k">return</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">c</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">getAuthenticationManager</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="p">}</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nd">@Bean</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">CorsConfigurationSource</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nf">corsConfigurationSource</span><span class="p">()</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="kd">var</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">cfg</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">CorsConfiguration</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="n">cfg</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">setAllowedOrigins</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">List</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">of</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"https://app.example.com"</span><span class="p">));</span><span class="w">   </span><span class="c1">// never "*" with credentials</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="n">cfg</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">setAllowedMethods</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">List</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">of</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"GET"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"POST"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"PUT"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"DELETE"</span><span class="p">));</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="n">cfg</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">setAllowedHeaders</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">List</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">of</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"Authorization"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="s">"Content-Type"</span><span class="p">));</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="n">cfg</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">setAllowCredentials</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kc">true</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="kd">var</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">src</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">UrlBasedCorsConfigurationSource</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="n">src</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">registerCorsConfiguration</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/**"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">cfg</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="k">return</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">src</span><span class="p">;</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="p">}</span>
<span class="p">}</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Multiple chains:</strong> declare several <code>SecurityFilterChain</code> beans with <code>@Order</code> and <code>securityMatcher</code> — e.g. a stateless JWT chain for <code>/api/**</code> and a form-login chain for an admin UI.</p>
<h2 id="p7-b3-questions-they-actually-ask">B3. Questions they actually ask<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p7-b3-questions-they-actually-ask">#</a></h2>
<section class="qa" id="q7-1"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q1</span><span class="qtext">How does Spring Security know a user's roles?</span></p><div class="a"><p><code>UserDetails.getAuthorities()</code> returns <code>GrantedAuthority</code>s. With JWT, the <code>JwtAuthenticationConverter</code> maps claims (<code>scope</code>, <code>roles</code>, or a custom claim) to authorities.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-2"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q2</span><span class="qtext"><code>hasRole</code> vs <code>hasAuthority</code>.</span></p><div class="a"><p><code>hasRole("ADMIN")</code> checks for the authority <code>ROLE_ADMIN</code> — the prefix is added for you. <code>hasAuthority("ROLE_ADMIN")</code> is the literal check. Mixing them up is the most common Spring Security bug. Prefer fine-grained authorities (<code>bet:place</code>) over coarse roles.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-3"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q3</span><span class="qtext">Method security — <code>@PreAuthorize</code> vs <code>@Secured</code> vs <code>@RolesAllowed</code>.</span></p><div class="a"><p><code>@PreAuthorize</code> supports SpEL and is the one to use: <code>@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN') or #userId == authentication.name")</code>. <code>@PostAuthorize</code> filters on the return value (<code>returnObject</code>). <code>@PreFilter</code>/<code>@PostFilter</code> filter collections. <code>@Secured</code> and <code>@RolesAllowed</code> are simple role lists with no SpEL.
<strong>Gotcha:</strong> method security is also proxy-based — self-invocation bypasses it.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-4"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q4</span><span class="qtext">Why <code>BCrypt</code>? What's a salt?</span></p><div class="a"><p>BCrypt is an adaptive hash with a tunable work factor and a <strong>per-password salt embedded in the output</strong>, so identical passwords hash differently and rainbow tables are useless. Increase the strength as hardware improves. Argon2 and SCrypt are also available; <code>DelegatingPasswordEncoder</code> (the default, <code>{bcrypt}$2a$...</code>) lets you migrate algorithms without breaking existing hashes.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-5"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q5</span><span class="qtext">Where do you get the current user?</span></p><div class="a"><div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="n">SecurityContextHolder</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">getContext</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="na">getAuthentication</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="c1">// or, cleanly, in a controller:</span>
<span class="nd">@GetMapping</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"/me"</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">String</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nf">me</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nd">@AuthenticationPrincipal</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Jwt</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">jwt</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">return</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">jwt</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">getSubject</span><span class="p">();</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">}</span>
</code></pre></div><p><code>SecurityContextHolder</code> is a <code>ThreadLocal</code> — so it is <strong>not</strong> propagated to <code>@Async</code> threads unless you set <code>SecurityContextHolder.setStrategyName(MODE_INHERITABLETHREADLOCAL)</code> or use <code>DelegatingSecurityContextExecutor</code>. A real production gotcha.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-6"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q6</span><span class="qtext">Stateless JWT auth — walk me through it.</span></p><div class="a"><p>Login endpoint validates credentials via <code>AuthenticationManager</code> → issues a short-lived access token (5–15 min, signed RS256) + a longer refresh token (stored server-side/rotated) → the client sends <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code> → <code>BearerTokenAuthenticationFilter</code> validates signature, <code>exp</code>, <code>iss</code>, <code>aud</code> against the JWKS endpoint → populates the <code>SecurityContext</code> → <code>AuthorizationFilter</code> checks authorities. No session, so it scales horizontally with no sticky sessions.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-7"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q7</span><span class="qtext">How do you revoke a JWT before it expires?</span></p><div class="a"><p>You can't, inherently — that's the trade-off for statelessness. Mitigations: short TTL, a denylist of <code>jti</code> in Redis checked on each request (reintroduces state, but a tiny amount), a <code>tokenVersion</code> claim compared against the user record, or rotate the signing key to invalidate everything.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-8"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q8</span><span class="qtext">CSRF — when do you disable it, and when must you not?</span></p><div class="a"><p>CSRF is only exploitable when the browser attaches credentials <strong>automatically</strong> — i.e. cookie or basic auth. A stateless API using an <code>Authorization</code> header is not vulnerable, so disabling is correct there. If you store the JWT in a cookie, you <strong>do</strong> need CSRF protection (or <code>SameSite=Strict/Lax</code>). Never disable it for a session-based server-rendered app.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-9"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q9</span><span class="qtext">CORS vs CSRF — how are they different?</span></p><div class="a"><p>CORS is a browser mechanism that <em>relaxes</em> the same-origin policy for reads; CSRF is an attack exploiting automatic credential attachment on writes. CORS does not protect you from CSRF — a simple POST doesn't even trigger a preflight.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-10"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q10</span><span class="qtext">Why does my CORS config not work when a request is unauthorised?</span></p><div class="a"><p>CORS must be handled <strong>before</strong> the security filters reject the request, otherwise the browser sees a 401 with no CORS headers and reports a CORS error. <code>http.cors()</code> places <code>CorsFilter</code> correctly; a hand-rolled filter usually needs <code>@Order(Ordered.HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)</code>.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-11"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q11</span><span class="qtext">OAuth2 grant types.</span></p><div class="a"><p><strong>Authorization Code + PKCE</strong> — the correct flow for web and mobile apps today. <strong>Client Credentials</strong> — machine-to-machine (service calling service). <strong>Refresh Token</strong>. <em>Implicit</em> and <em>Password</em> grants are deprecated. Know the roles: resource owner, client, authorization server, resource server.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-12"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q12</span><span class="qtext">OIDC vs OAuth2.</span></p><div class="a"><p>OAuth2 is authorisation (delegated access); OIDC is an identity layer on top adding the <code>id_token</code>, <code>/userinfo</code>, and standard claims. "OAuth2 for permissions, OIDC for login."</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-13"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q13</span><span class="qtext">Security headers Spring adds by default.</span></p><div class="a"><p><code>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>, <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code> (clickjacking), <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code>, HSTS on HTTPS. Add <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> yourself — it's the strongest XSS defence.</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-14"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q14</span><span class="qtext">OWASP Top 10 — name a few and the Spring mitigation.</span></p><div class="a"><p>Broken access control (method security + deny-by-default), injection (parameterised queries / JPA; never string-concatenate SQL or JPQL), cryptographic failures (BCrypt, TLS, no secrets in logs), insecure design, security misconfiguration (don't expose all Actuator endpoints), vulnerable components (dependency scanning), identification/auth failures (rate-limit login, lock accounts, MFA), SSRF (validate outbound URLs), logging failures (audit auth events).</p></div></section><section class="qa" id="q7-15"><p class="q"><span class="qnum">Q15</span><span class="qtext">How do you test a secured endpoint?</span></p><div class="a"><p><code>@WithMockUser(roles="ADMIN")</code>, <code>@WithAnonymousUser</code>, <code>SecurityMockMvcRequestPostProcessors.jwt()</code>, or <code>@WithUserDetails</code>.</p></div></section><hr/>
<h1>SECTION C — Configuration: <code>application.yml</code> and Properties</h1>
<h2 id="p7-c1-property-source-precedence-highest-wins">C1. Property source precedence (highest wins)<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p7-c1-property-source-precedence-highest-wins">#</a></h2>
<ol>
<li>Devtools settings in <code>~/.config/spring-boot</code></li>
<li><code>@TestPropertySource</code> / test <code>properties</code> attribute</li>
<li><strong>Command-line arguments</strong> (<code>--server.port=9090</code>)</li>
<li><code>SPRING_APPLICATION_JSON</code> (inline JSON in an env var)</li>
<li><code>ServletConfig</code> / <code>ServletContext</code> params</li>
<li>JNDI</li>
<li><strong>Java system properties</strong> (<code>-Dserver.port=9090</code>)</li>
<li><strong>OS environment variables</strong></li>
<li>Profile-specific application properties <strong>outside</strong> the jar</li>
<li>Profile-specific application properties <strong>inside</strong> the jar</li>
<li>Application properties outside the jar</li>
<li>Application properties inside the jar</li>
<li><code>@PropertySource</code> on <code>@Configuration</code></li>
<li><code>SpringApplication.setDefaultProperties</code></li>
</ol>
<p>The practical takeaway: <strong>env vars and command-line args override packaged config</strong> — which is exactly how you configure the same image differently per environment in Kubernetes.</p>
<p><strong>Relaxed binding:</strong> <code>app.betting.max-stake</code>, <code>app.betting.maxStake</code>, <code>APP_BETTING_MAXSTAKE</code> all bind to the same property. Env vars use uppercase with underscores; that's the K8s/Docker path.</p>
<h2 id="p7-c2-a-realistic-application-yml">C2. A realistic <code>application.yml</code><a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p7-c2-a-realistic-application-yml">#</a></h2>
<div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="nt">spring</span><span class="p">:</span>
