<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">username</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">${DB_USER}</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">password</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">${DB_PASSWORD}</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">hikari</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">maximum-pool-size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">20</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">minimum-idle</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">5</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">connection-timeout</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">3000</span><span class="w">      </span><span class="c1"># fail fast rather than pile up</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">max-lifetime</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">1200000</span><span class="w">         </span><span class="c1"># must be shorter than the DB/network idle timeout</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">leak-detection-threshold</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">20000</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">jpa</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">hibernate</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">ddl-auto</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">validate</span><span class="w">            </span><span class="c1"># never 'update' in production</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">open-in-view</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">false</span><span class="w">             </span><span class="c1"># turn this OFF — it holds connections for the whole request</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">properties</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">hibernate</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">        </span><span class="nt">jdbc.batch_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">50</span>
<span class="w">        </span><span class="nt">order_inserts</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span>
<span class="w">        </span><span class="nt">order_updates</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span>
<span class="w">        </span><span class="nt">query.in_clause_parameter_padding</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">show-sql</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">false</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">flyway</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">enabled</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">baseline-on-migrate</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">kafka</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">bootstrap-servers</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">${KAFKA_BROKERS}</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">producer</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">acks</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">all</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">properties.enable.idempotence</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">consumer</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">group-id</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">bet-placement</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">auto-offset-reset</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">earliest</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">enable-auto-commit</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">false</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">max-poll-records</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">100</span>

<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">jackson</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">default-property-inclusion</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">non_null</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">serialization</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">write-dates-as-timestamps</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">false</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">fail-on-empty-beans</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">false</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">deserialization</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">fail-on-unknown-properties</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">false</span>

<span class="nt">server</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">port</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">8080</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">shutdown</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">graceful</span><span class="w">                </span><span class="c1"># drain in-flight requests on SIGTERM</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">compression.enabled</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">tomcat</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">threads.max</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">200</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">max-connections</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">8192</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">accept-count</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">100</span>

<span class="nt">management</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">endpoints.web.exposure.include</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">health,info,metrics,prometheus,loggers</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">endpoint.health</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">show-details</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">when-authorized</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">probes.enabled</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">true</span><span class="w">            </span><span class="c1"># /health/liveness and /health/readiness for K8s</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">metrics.tags.application</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">${spring.application.name}</span>

<span class="nt">logging</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">level</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">root</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">INFO</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">com.entain.bets</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">DEBUG</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">org.hibernate.SQL</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">WARN</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">pattern</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">console</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">"%d{ISO8601}</span><span class="nv"> </span><span class="s">%-5level</span><span class="nv"> </span><span class="s">[%X{traceId}]</span><span class="nv"> </span><span class="s">%logger{36}</span><span class="nv"> </span><span class="s">-</span><span class="nv"> </span><span class="s">%msg%n"</span>

<span class="nt">app</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">betting</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">max-stake</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">5000.00</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">odds-tolerance</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">0.05</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">markets</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p p-Indicator">-</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">football</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="p p-Indicator">-</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">tennis</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">limits</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">vip</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">50000</span>
<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">standard</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">5000</span>

<span class="nn">---</span>
<span class="nt">spring</span><span class="p">:</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">config.activate.on-profile</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">prod</span><span class="w">      </span><span class="c1"># profile-specific block in the same file</span>
<span class="w">  </span><span class="nt">jpa.show-sql</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">false</span>
<span class="nt">logging.level.com.entain.bets</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">INFO</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>Notes worth mentioning aloud: <code>---</code> separates profile documents in one YAML file (the modern key is <code>spring.config.activate.on-profile</code>, not the deprecated <code>spring.profiles</code>); <code>${VAR:default}</code> gives an env var with a fallback; <code>spring.config.import</code> pulls in Config Server, Vault, or extra files.</p>
<h2 id="p7-c3-value-vs-configurationproperties">C3. <code>@Value</code> vs <code>@ConfigurationProperties</code><a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p7-c3-value-vs-configurationproperties">#</a></h2>
<div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="nd">@Component</span>
<span class="nd">@ConfigurationProperties</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">prefix</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">"app.betting"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="nd">@Validated</span>
<span class="kd">public</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">class</span> <span class="nc">BettingProperties</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="nd">@NotNull</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nd">@DecimalMin</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"0.01"</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">private</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">BigDecimal</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">maxStake</span><span class="p">;</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="kd">private</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">BigDecimal</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">oddsTolerance</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">BigDecimal</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"0.05"</span><span class="p">);</span><span class="w">   </span><span class="c1">// default</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="kd">private</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">List</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">markets</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">ArrayList</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="kd">private</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Map</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">BigDecimal</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">limits</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">new</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HashMap</span><span class="o">&lt;&gt;</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="c1">// getters + setters required for binding (or use a @ConstructorBinding record)</span>
<span class="p">}</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>Or as an immutable record (Boot 3 — <code>@ConstructorBinding</code> is inferred):</p>
<div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="nd">@ConfigurationProperties</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">prefix</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">"app.betting"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="kd">public</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">record</span> <span class="nc">BettingProperties</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">BigDecimal</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">maxStake</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">BigDecimal</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">oddsTolerance</span><span class="p">,</span>
<span class="w">                                </span><span class="n">List</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">markets</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Map</span><span class="o">&lt;</span><span class="n">String</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">BigDecimal</span><span class="o">&gt;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">limits</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{}</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Why prefer <code>@ConfigurationProperties</code>?</strong> Type-safe, hierarchical, supports validation, relaxed binding, IDE autocompletion via the metadata processor, and testable as a plain object. <code>@Value</code> is fine for one-offs but scatters config strings across the codebase and <strong>doesn't work in constructors of the same bean or in <code>@PostConstruct</code> when field-injected</strong>.</p>
<h2 id="p7-c4-profiles">C4. Profiles<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p7-c4-profiles">#</a></h2>
<p><code>spring.profiles.active=prod,eu-west</code>, or <code>SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE</code> in the container. <code>spring.profiles.include</code> layers extras. <code>spring.profiles.group.prod=prod,metrics,secure</code> composes groups (Boot 2.4+). <code>@Profile("!prod")</code> on a bean for local mocks. Files: <code>application-prod.yml</code> beside <code>application.yml</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Common question:</strong> <em>"How do you manage config across dev/QA/prod?"</em> → One image, config injected per environment via env vars/ConfigMaps; secrets from Vault or Secrets Manager, never in the repo; Spring Cloud Config Server with git-backed versioning if you need central management and refresh; <code>@RefreshScope</code> + <code>/actuator/refresh</code> for runtime changes.</p>
<hr/>
<h1>SECTION D — Runtime &amp; Remaining Concepts</h1>
<p><strong>D1. What actually happens on <code>SpringApplication.run()</code>?</strong>
Create the <code>ApplicationContext</code> → load <code>ApplicationContextInitializer</code>s and listeners from spring.factories → prepare the <code>Environment</code> (property sources, profiles) → print the banner → register bean definitions → run <code>BeanFactoryPostProcessor</code>s → instantiate singletons → apply <code>BeanPostProcessor</code>s (AOP proxies created here) → start the embedded server → fire <code>ApplicationReadyEvent</code> → run <code>CommandLineRunner</code>/<code>ApplicationRunner</code> beans.</p>
<p><strong>D2. Application events.</strong>
<code>ApplicationStartingEvent</code> → <code>ApplicationEnvironmentPreparedEvent</code> → <code>ApplicationContextInitializedEvent</code> → <code>ApplicationPreparedEvent</code> → <code>ContextRefreshedEvent</code> → <code>ApplicationStartedEvent</code> → <code>ApplicationReadyEvent</code> → <code>ApplicationFailedEvent</code>. Use <code>ApplicationReadyEvent</code> for warm-up work, not <code>@PostConstruct</code>.</p>
<p><strong>D3. <code>CommandLineRunner</code> vs <code>ApplicationRunner</code>.</strong> Same purpose; the former takes <code>String...</code>, the latter takes parsed <code>ApplicationArguments</code>. Both run after the context is ready; order with <code>@Order</code>.</p>
<p><strong>D4. Filter vs Interceptor vs AOP vs <code>@ControllerAdvice</code> — which and when?</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Filter</strong> (servlet level) — runs before Spring MVC, sees raw request/response; use for CORS, security, request logging, correlation IDs, compression.</li>
<li><strong>HandlerInterceptor</strong> (Spring MVC level) — knows the handler method; <code>preHandle</code>/<code>postHandle</code>/<code>afterCompletion</code>; use for auth checks tied to controllers, timing, locale.</li>
<li><strong>AOP aspect</strong> — any Spring bean method; use for cross-cutting business concerns (audit, retry, metrics).</li>
<li><strong><code>@ControllerAdvice</code></strong> — exception handling and global model attributes.
Order: Filter → Interceptor → Aspect → Controller.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>D5. Embedded server and thread model.</strong>
Tomcat by default (Jetty/Undertow are swappable). One request = one thread from a pool of 200. Blocking IO means a slow downstream saturates the pool → tune <code>server.tomcat.threads.max</code>, add timeouts, bulkheads, or move to WebFlux/virtual threads.
<strong>Boot 3.2+:</strong> <code>spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true</code> runs request handling on virtual threads — thread-per-request that scales to blocking IO. Caveat: <code>synchronized</code> blocks pin the carrier thread; use <code>ReentrantLock</code>.</p>
<p><strong>D6. Graceful shutdown.</strong> <code>server.shutdown=graceful</code> + <code>spring.lifecycle.timeout-per-shutdown-phase=30s</code>. On SIGTERM the server stops accepting new requests and lets in-flight ones finish — essential for zero-downtime rolling deploys in K8s (pair with a <code>preStop</code> sleep so the load balancer deregisters first).</p>
<p><strong>D7. Actuator: custom health and metrics.</strong></p>
<div class="hl"><pre><span></span><code><span class="nd">@Component</span>
<span class="kd">public</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">class</span> <span class="nc">OddsFeedHealthIndicator</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kd">implements</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">HealthIndicator</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="kd">public</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Health</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nf">health</span><span class="p">()</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="p">{</span>
<span class="w">        </span><span class="k">return</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">feed</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">isConnected</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="w">            </span><span class="o">?</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Health</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">up</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="na">withDetail</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"lastTick"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">feed</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">lastTick</span><span class="p">()).</span><span class="na">build</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="w">            </span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">Health</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">down</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="na">withDetail</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"reason"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">"feed disconnected"</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">build</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="w">    </span><span class="p">}</span>
<span class="p">}</span>
<span class="c1">// custom metric</span>
<span class="n">Counter</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">builder</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"bets.placed"</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">tag</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"market"</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">marketId</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">register</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">meterRegistry</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">increment</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="n">Timer</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="na">builder</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"bets.placement.latency"</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">register</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">meterRegistry</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="na">record</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">duration</span><span class="p">);</span>
</code></pre></div>
<p>Map health groups to probes: <code>management.endpoint.health.group.readiness.include=db,kafka</code>. Keep liveness cheap — a liveness check that touches the DB will restart every pod during a DB blip.</p>
<p><strong>D8. Logging.</strong> SLF4J API + Logback by default. Use parameterised logging (<code>log.debug("bet {} rejected: {}", id, reason)</code>) — never string concatenation, which builds the string even when the level is off. JSON encoder for log aggregation. Correlation IDs via MDC (<code>MDC.put("traceId", ...)</code>) — <strong>always clear it in a finally block</strong>, since pooled threads are reused. Change levels at runtime via <code>/actuator/loggers</code>.</p>
<p><strong>D9. Jackson.</strong> <code>@JsonProperty</code>, <code>@JsonIgnore</code>, <code>@JsonInclude(NON_NULL)</code>, <code>@JsonFormat(pattern=)</code>, <code>@JsonCreator</code>/<code>@JsonValue</code>, <code>@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown=true)</code>, <code>@JsonManagedReference</code>/<code>@JsonBackReference</code> for bidirectional relations, custom <code>JsonSerializer</code>. Register <code>JavaTimeModule</code> (Boot does it) and set <code>write-dates-as-timestamps: false</code> so you get ISO-8601.</p>
<p><strong>D10. Spring Boot 3 migration — what changed?</strong>
Java 17 baseline; <code>javax.*</code> → <code>jakarta.*</code> (the big one); <code>WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter</code> removed; Micrometer Observation API replaces Sleuth; native image support via GraalVM AOT; <code>spring.factories</code> replaced by <code>AutoConfiguration.imports</code>; <code>ProblemDetail</code> (RFC 7807) built in; <code>HttpExchange</code> declarative HTTP clients; Boot 3.2 adds virtual threads and <code>RestClient</code>.</p>
<p><strong>D11. WebFlux vs MVC — when would you use it?</strong>
WebFlux (Reactor: <code>Mono</code>/<code>Flux</code>, Netty, event loop) for high-concurrency IO-bound workloads, streaming, and when the whole stack is non-blocking. Costs: steeper learning curve, harder debugging, blocking JDBC ruins it (needs R2DBC). With virtual threads in Boot 3.2+, the case for reactive purely for scalability is much weaker — say this, it's the current industry view.</p>
<p><strong>D12. Common startup failures and their causes.</strong>
<code>NoSuchBeanDefinitionException</code> (component outside the scanned package, or a missing <code>@Component</code>), <code>BeanCurrentlyInCreationException</code> (circular dependency — fix with <code>@Lazy</code> or by redesigning), <code>Port already in use</code>, <code>Failed to configure a DataSource</code> (a DB starter on the classpath with no URL — add config or exclude the auto-config), <code>NoUniqueBeanDefinitionException</code> (needs <code>@Primary</code>/<code>@Qualifier</code>).</p>
<hr/>
<h1>SECTION E — Rapid self-test</h1>
<ol>
<li>What three annotations does <code>@SpringBootApplication</code> combine?</li>
<li>Why does <code>@Repository</code> do more than <code>@Service</code>?</li>
