<h2 id="p8-4-the-stream-pipeline">4. The stream pipeline<a aria-label="Link to this section" class="anchor" href="#p8-4-the-stream-pipeline">#</a></h2>
<p>A stream is not a collection. It holds no data, it's traversed once, and <strong>nothing runs until the terminal operation</strong>.</p>
<figure class="fig-wrap">
<svg aria-label="Stream pipeline stages" class="fig" role="img" viewbox="0 0 720 230" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<defs><marker id="ah3" markerheight="9" markerwidth="9" orient="auto" refx="8" refy="4.5">
<path class="fill-ln" d="M0,1 L8,4.5 L0,8 z"></path></marker></defs>
<rect class="box" height="58" rx="5" width="118" x="14" y="52"></rect>
<text class="t ctr" x="73" y="76">Source</text>
<text class="m ctr" x="73" y="96">stream()</text>
<line class="ln" marker-end="url(#ah3)" x1="132" x2="168" y1="81" y2="81"></line>
<rect class="qbox" height="58" rx="5" width="118" x="172" y="52"></rect>
<text class="t ctr" x="231" y="76">filter</text>
<text class="m ctr" x="231" y="96">lazy</text>
<line class="ln" marker-end="url(#ah3)" x1="290" x2="326" y1="81" y2="81"></line>
<rect class="qbox" height="58" rx="5" width="118" x="330" y="52"></rect>
<text class="t ctr" x="389" y="76">map</text>
<text class="m ctr" x="389" y="96">lazy</text>
<line class="ln" marker-end="url(#ah3)" x1="448" x2="484" y1="81" y2="81"></line>
<rect class="abox" height="58" rx="5" width="140" x="488" y="52"></rect>
<text class="t ctr" x="558" y="76">collect</text>
<text class="m ctr" x="558" y="96">terminal — runs it</text>
<text class="st ctr" x="231" y="30">intermediate</text>
<text class="st ctr" x="389" y="30">intermediate</text>
<text class="st ctr" x="558" y="30">terminal</text>
<text class="st" x="14" y="150">One element at a time, all the way through — not stage by stage. So</text>
<text class="st" x="14" y="170"><tspan class="mono">findFirst()</tspan> can stop after the first match instead of mapping the whole list.</text>
<text class="st" x="14" y="200">Stateful ops (<tspan class="mono">sorted</tspan>, <tspan class="mono">distinct</tspan>) break that: they must buffer everything before emitting.</text>
</svg>
<figcaption>Build the pipeline, then pull. Without a terminal operation, none of the lambdas ever execute.</figcaption>
</figure>
