<section class="panel" id="panel-11" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-11" hidden><header class="part-head"><span class="part-n">Part 11</span><h1>Long-form Answers &amp; Code</h1><p class="kicker">Spoken versions, solutions <span class="dot">·</span> 39 questions</p></header><div class="prose">
<blockquote>
<p>Part 10 lists what candidates were asked. This part answers it.
Two kinds of content here: <strong>spoken answers</strong> — the 45–90 second version you'd actually say out loud for the highest-frequency items — and <strong>the gaps</strong>, meaning reported questions that aren't covered anywhere else in this kit (service registry internals, API gateway routing, config server, DNS, ELK internals, Jenkins, Saga drawbacks, Kafka consumer failure). Plus working code for every reported coding problem.</p>
